<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62983" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῃστ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>, ὁ, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ληϊστής</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λᾳστής</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ληΐς, ληΐζομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>robber, pirate</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				766
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				2.4.23
			</span></i>, etc.; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλέπτης</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				351c
			</span></i>; esp. by sea, <i>buccaneer</i>, later <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πειρατής</span>, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.138
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῃστοῦ βίον ζῆν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					507e
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ληϊστὴς κατεστήκεε
			Καρχηδονίων</span> he began a course of <i>piracies</i> upon
			them, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.17
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ λ. αὑτοὺς ποριστὰς καλοῦσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1405a25
				</span></i>
			; of irregular troops, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(2).526
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Eresos</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ἐναργὴς τῆς ἐμῆς τυραννίδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					535
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύπριδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					1143
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῃστὰ λογισμοῦ</span>, of love, <i><span class="en">
				<u>APl.</u>
				4.198
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Maec.
			</span></i>).</div>
